# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. A CRLF shebang line (`#!/bin/zsh\r`)
# makes macOS and Linux fail the script with "bad interpreter", and this repo
# is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise flip
# them on checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf

# HTML test fixtures must keep LF endings too: the network log prints a page's
# Content-Length, so a CRLF checkout of e2e-playground.html (12 914 -> 13 168
# bytes) turns the NET-1 row's "12.6 KB" into "12.9 KB" (wave W1 probe,
# 2026-10-22; decisions.md · NET-1's 12.9 KB came from a CRLF copy of the fixture).
test-fixtures/**/*.html text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts keep LF endings too: several recipe tests read a .ps1 as text
# and match it line by line, and a fresh Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) turned
# them CRLF, which failed 9 tests in recipes/test/s11-r16-runner.test.ts (Step 14
# Stage 0). PowerShell 5.1 runs LF scripts as is.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
